Package: snic
Type: Package
Title: Superpixel Segmentation with the SNIC Algorithm
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Rolf", family = "Simoes", email = "rolfsimoes@gmail.com", 
    role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person('Felipe', 'Souza', role = c('ctb'), email = 'felipe.carvalho@inpe.br'),
    person('Felipe', 'Carlos', role = c('ctb'), email = "efelipecarlos@gmail.com"),
    person('Gilberto', 'Camara', role = c('ctb', 'rth'), email = 'gilberto.camara.inpe@gmail.com')
    )
Description: Implementation of the Simple Non-Iterative Clustering (SNIC) 
    algorithm for superpixel segmentation of multi-band images.  The core 
    algorithm is written in C++ and exposed to R via a small interface.  
    The implementation uses a priority queue (min-heap) to grow compact, 
    homogeneous segments from uniformly distributed seeds.  Supports 
    images with an arbitrary number of spectral bands and returns an integer 
    matrix of segment labels covering the input scene.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
